{"id":"n3-123","title":"～わけではない","romaji":"〜wake dewa nai","jlptLevel":3,"shortExplanation":"Denies a general assumption; 'it does not mean that', 'it's not the case'.","longExplanation":"The ～わけではない grammar point is used to deny or correct a general assumption or statement without completely negating the situation. It often emphasizes one particular point that is not true, while acknowledging other possibilities.","formation":"Verb-casual + わけではない, い-Adjective + わけではない, な-Adjective + だわけではない, Noun + だわけではない","examples":[{"jp":"彼が忙しいからといって、友達がいないわけではない。","romaji":"Kare ga isogashii kara to itte, tomodachi ga inai wake dewa nai.","en":"Just because he's busy doesn't mean he has no friends.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"忙しい","vocabId":"1519290","reading":"いそがしい"},{"surface":"から","vocabId":null},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いう"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"友達","vocabId":"1540170","reading":"ともだち"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"わけ","vocabId":"1538330","reading":"わけ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[12,13,14,15]},{"jp":"この映画は面白くないわけではないが、好みではない。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa omoshirokunai wake dewa nai ga, konomi dewa nai.","en":"It's not that this movie isn't interesting; it's just not my taste.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"映画","vocabId":"1173720","reading":"えいが"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"面白く","vocabId":"1533580","reading":"おもしろい","baseForm":"面白い"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"わけ","vocabId":"1538330","reading":"わけ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":"2